## API

All endpoints are under `/api/v1/`. Send the access token as `Authorization: Bearer <access>`.

| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| POST | `auth/register/` | – | Create an account |
| POST | `auth/login/` | – | Log in with email and password |
| POST | `auth/logout/` | ✓ | Blacklist a refresh token |
| POST | `auth/token/refresh/` | – | Swap a refresh token for new tokens |
{% if two_factor %}
| POST | `auth/otp/verify/` | – | Verify an emailed code, receive tokens |
| POST | `auth/otp/resend/` | – | Send a new code |
{% endif %}
| GET / PATCH | `auth/me/` | ✓ | Read or update your profile |
| POST | `auth/password/change/` | ✓ | Change your password |
| POST | `auth/password/reset/` | – | Email a password reset link |
| POST | `auth/password/reset/confirm/` | – | Set a new password with `uid` and `token` from the link |
| GET | `users/` | admin | List users (`?search=`, `?ordering=`, `?page=`) |
| GET / PATCH | `users/<id>/` | admin | View a user or change their `role` and `is_active` |

A successful login returns:

```json
{
  "user": {"id": 1, "email": "jane@example.com", "name": "Jane Doe"},
  "tokens": {"access": "...", "refresh": "..."}
}
```

Errors always have the same shape:

```json
{"message": "Passwords do not match.", "code": "invalid", "errors": {"password_confirm": ["Passwords do not match."]}}
```
{% if two_factor %}

### Email verification and two-factor login

1. `register` creates the account and emails a code. The response contains
   `"requires_otp": true` and a `verification_id`, but no tokens.
2. `login` checks the password. If the email isn't verified yet, or the user has
   `two_factor_enabled`, it emails a code and returns a `verification_id`
   instead of tokens.
3. `otp/verify` with `{"verification_id": "...", "code": "123456"}` returns the
   tokens.
4. `otp/resend` with `{"verification_id": "..."}` sends a new code and returns a
   new `verification_id`. There is a cooldown between resends.

Codes are stored hashed and can only be used once. They expire after
`OTP_EXPIRY_MINUTES` and lock after `OTP_MAX_ATTEMPTS` wrong tries. Users turn
two-factor login on or off with `PATCH auth/me/ {"two_factor_enabled": true}`.
{% endif %}
